    "done_when": "Three narrowings in reckon/crew/promotion.py and reckon/cli.py, each with a named test in tests/test_bookkeeping_follows_the_run.py, which passes at exit 0. (1) A run whose record carries attempt_kind resume or redispatch promotes with impl_move recorded as exempt, so no --no-impl-change is needed; the --repairs declaration is a later node and is out of scope here. (2) A review run's --outcome is optional and defaults to its stored review's total score and finding count. (3) verify-gate accepts a checkout when the merged revision is an ancestor of the checkout's HEAD and none of the run's changed paths differs between the two, tested on a checkout two ledger commits past the merge; a checkout where a changed path differs is still refused. tests/test_promotion_requires_impl_move.py and tests/test_verify_gate_command_option.py pass, and the manifest records base and head arms of the three files, each log header printing its revision and reckon.__file__. The manifest cites the reuse map at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s25-coord/s25-reuse-map-record-and-promotion/reuse-map.md for _require_impl_moved, the --outcome refusal and rerun_gate_at_integrated_revision, re-derived at its own base. The declared negative control is applied, the two-commits-past case is observed to be refused, and that log's absolute path is in the manifest.",
